(D/'DERIVATION.md').write_text("""# Mechanism-resolved four axes
Let T=max_A t_a true minimax WDL in [-1,1], T_K=max_K t_a, H_K=max_K h_a, H_A=max_A h_a. Legacy refined v_alpha=(1-alpha)v+alpha H_K. Exact signed error identity:
v_alpha-T=(1-alpha)(v-T)+alpha[(T_K-T)+(H_K-T_K)].
Omission T_K-T<=0. The max-estimation term can have either sign for a fixed leaf; if all h_a unbiased in a specified conditional ensemble, E H_K>=T_K by Jensen (fixed K or conditional unbiasedness given K); no guarantee for deterministic trained NN errors, adaptive K, or biased estimates. |H_K-T_K|<=max_K|h_a-t_a|. Alternative H_A removes omission but increases evaluations and can amplify noise. Exact certificate: for each terminal child t_a=-outcome(child), unknown children interval [-1,1]. max lower <= T <= max upper. If any terminal winning action or all legal children terminal, interval collapses (also one-step draw/loss only under complete coverage except a winning action); propagate exact leaf evaluation without B shrink on that trajectory. This is not a solved root or a recursive MCTS solver. Proof-only scans all legal children and no extra NN. TOP2/FULL scan all for proof then evaluate subset/full if |v|<=.65 and >=2 legal; half blend otherwise. LEGACY retains original top2 no proof priority. Priors unchanged. A proof changes leaf value, not visit accounting. Example t=(1,-1,-1), selected K=(2,3), h=t: omission -2; full exact; no noise. Two unbiased Rademacher estimates for t=(0,0): expected max=.5. Two estimates can also share perfect correlation, expected max=0.
B split: B0 original; B1 serialized n/W/M2 writer no value blending; B2 own-context raw mean only; B3 other-context raw mean only; B4 other preferred, own fallback as previous. For target theta, errors e=y-theta, f=m-theta. s=E e^2, t=E f^2, r=E ef (includes bias; same conditioning). MSE of (1-eta)y+eta m equals s+2eta(r-s)+eta^2(s+t-2r). Denominator D=E(e-f)^2>=0. If D>0 unconstrained eta*=(s-r)/D, clip to [0,1/4]. If D=0, errors equal a.s., mixing cannot improve. Necessary for infinitesimal benefit r<s; for finite eta>0 improve iff 2(s-r)>eta D. If correlation/bias high, provenance is insufficient to imply benefit. No variance reduction claim from incoming count alone. Exact terminal/certified trajectories unchanged; append one raw return per edge, no pseudo counts. B1 isolates coherent writes (RTT diagnostic disabled for all B1–4; unused in this config); weak reads remain. Shared TT state is identified by native key; verify distinct-context toy fixture and actual telemetry, not collision-free theorem. Use fixed eta from previous experiment, not estimate MSE from selected TEST.
S/X frozen, compare base and SX; phase interventions after common deterministic eight-visit prefix within same SX configuration. X changes initial materialization, hence BASE vs SX not identical prefix. Within SX arms identical prefix, B ledger starts at intervention (no reconstructed historical B data), compare actual two-thread continuations. Model goal is eventual joint VOC, not fixed control optimization. For resource comparison, stop at synchronous chunk boundaries, fixed 64 visits or NN call target or common total-elapsed target plus visit cap; record realized overshoot, terminal-driven saturation, setup/drop and whole cost. Equal targets are not automatically equal realized resources.
""")
